text:
Looking at the board: Russia confirmed F RUM supports A SER - BUD. Italy threatened A BUD - SER and A VIE - GAL simultaneously, but that would be reckless overextension. Turkey declined to move A BUL - GRE. My plan is A SER - BUD (with Russian support) and A GAL holds. I need to lock in Russia's commitment and warn Italy off the double-attack.

MESSAGES:
{
  "RUSSIA": "Final confirmation: I'm ordering A SER - BUD this fall and need F RUM S A SER - BUD. A GAL holds — no threat to WAR or RUM. If Italy does push A BUD - SER, your support still sends me into BUD while Italy bounces back into nothing; we both win.",
  "ITALY": "If you push A BUD - SER and A VIE - GAL simultaneously, Russia's F RUM supports me into BUD while you vacate it — you end up with neither BUD nor SER and I'm back at 3 centers. Hold BUD and VIE in place; the board punishes that overextension more than it punishes me."
}

Final round. England is committed to HOL with F DEN support, which pins A HOL. Germany says A HOL isn't contesting BEL. My BEL strike (F PIC - BEL + A BUR support) should land clean. Let me lock in with England and reassure Germany so he keeps A HOL pinned/passive.

MESSAGES:
{
  "ENGLAND": "Locked: F PIC - BEL with A BUR supporting, strength 2. You drive F NTH - HOL with F DEN supporting — that pins A HOL so it can't contest BEL, and you take HOL. Do NOT send anything into BEL. We both grow and Germany drops to 3.",
  "GERMANY": "Confirmed: I hold A BUR in place and take only BEL, leaving KIE/BER/MUN untouched this year. Keep A HOL out of BEL as you said — England is hitting HOL anyway, so defending BEL only loses you the unit for nothing. Clean border holds while you press Italy south."
}

I'm boxed at 7 with England holding the Atlantic. My best concrete gain this fall is BEL: it's empty, and I can take it with A PIC→BEL supported by F HOL. The question is whether England's F ENG contests BEL. I need to deter him and seize the empty center. Let me close with England honestly-framed (I'm taking the empty BEL, don't fight me there) and keep Germany as buffer.

MESSAGES:
{
  "ENGLAND": "I'm taking the empty BEL this fall with A PIC supported by F HOL — it's an undefended center and I won't sit at 7 while you build north. Keep F ENG out of BEL and the rest of our western line stays clean; I take no swing at your home fleets. Move F ENG into BEL and you've chosen a real war, so decide whether one province is worth that.",
  "GERMANY": "Border stays clean — I touch neither BER nor MUN. I'm pushing A PIC into BEL this turn, which pins England's western fleets; keep your units harassing England's KIE/north so his stack can't consolidate. That's mutual survival."
}
